# Standalone Binary Reverse Engineering (Zero-MCP)

This skill provides a complete, self-contained reverse engineering workflow using native Linux CLI tools and standard Python libraries. Use this when the REA MCP server is offline, when working in lightweight environments, or for fast single-binary checks without MCP overhead.

---

## 🛠️ Toolchain Matrix

| Target Format | Primary Tool | Command Pattern | Key Outputs |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Linux ELF (`.so`, `.ko`, exec)** | `readelf` + `objdump` | `readelf -Ws <elf>`, `objdump -d -M intel` | Symbols, PLT/GOT relocations, assembly |
| **Windows PE (`.exe`, `.dll`, ASI)** | Python `pefile` + `objdump` | Python script, `objdump -p <pe>` | Imports, Exports, Section entropy, RVA |
| **Android (`.apk`, `.dex`, `.jar`)** | `jadx` CLI | `jadx -d <outdir> --show-bad-code <apk>` | Readable Java classes, AndroidManifest.xml |
| **Game Archives & Custom Binaries** | `hexdump` / `strings` / Python | `xxd -l 128`, `strings -n 6` | Magic headers, section offsets, ASCII/UTF strings |
| **Dynamic / Memory Inspection** | `gdb` (batch mode) | `gdb -batch -ex "disas main" <binary>` | Function frame analysis, register mappings |

