## 1. Linux ELF Analysis (`readelf` & `objdump`)

### Quick Identification
```bash
file target.so
readelf -h target.so | grep -E "Class|Machine|Entry"
```

### Exported & Imported Symbols
```bash
# Clean demangled dynamic symbols
nm -D --demangle target.so | grep -E " [T|t] "

# Detailed symbol table with binding and visibility
readelf -Ws --demangle target.so | grep -E "FUNC|OBJECT"
```

### Relocations & PLT/GOT
```bash
readelf -r target.so
```

### Targeted Function Disassembly (Token-Safe)
Never dump entire binaries into terminal output. Disassemble only target functions:
```bash
objdump -d -M intel --no-show-raw-insn target.so | sed -n '/<target_function>:/,/^$/p' | head -n 50
```

