## 2. Windows PE & DLL Analysis (`pefile` & Python)

Inspect Windows executables and game DLLs (e.g. S.T.A.L.K.E.R., GTA, Unity plugins) using Python:

### Extract Exports, Imports, and Sections
```python
import pefile

pe = pefile.PE("target.dll")

# Print section headers
for section in pe.sections:
    print(f"{section.Name.decode().strip()}: VSize={hex(section.Misc_VirtualSize)} RawSize={hex(section.SizeOfRawData)}")

# Print imported DLLs and functions
if hasattr(pe, "DIRECTORY_ENTRY_IMPORT"):
    for entry in pe.DIRECTORY_ENTRY_IMPORT:
        print(f"Import from {entry.dll.decode()}:")
        for imp in entry.imports[:5]:
            print(f"  {hex(imp.address)}: {imp.name.decode() if imp.name else ord(imp.ordinal)}")

# Print exported functions
if hasattr(pe, "DIRECTORY_ENTRY_EXPORT"):
    for exp in pe.DIRECTORY_ENTRY_EXPORT.symbols:
        print(f"Export: {exp.name.decode() if exp.name else 'ord_' + str(exp.ordinal)} @ RVA {hex(exp.address)}")
```

